### CRIT-2: Hardcoded Live API Keys in Source Code

Even if [.env](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/.env) is properly secured, these LIVE production keys are embedded directly in TypeScript source code:

**File: [server/integrations/paddle/index.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/paddle/index.ts) (line 10)**
```typescript
const PADDLE_API_KEY = process.env.PADDLE_API_KEY || "pdl_live_apikey_01kjvyycf8yktbsvnwv75ynk64_28CEdjDMKVPSRm4ajHGAyx_AtC";
```

**File: [server/integrations/paddle/routes.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/paddle/routes.ts) (lines 17-18)**
```typescript
const PADDLE_PRICE_ID = process.env.PADDLE_PRICE_ID || "";
const PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN = process.env.PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN || "";
```

**Impact:** These keys are in source code which goes into git. Anyone with repo access (or if repo is public) gets live Paddle payment API access.

**Recommendation:** Remove all hardcoded fallback values. Use empty string `""` as fallback and fail fast with a clear error if the env var is missing.

