### CRIT-3: Session Secret is `dev-secret-change-in-production`

**File: [.env](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/.env) (line 12)**
```
SESSION_SECRET=dev-secret-change-in-production
```

**File: [server/integrations/auth/googleAuth.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/auth/googleAuth.ts) (line 27)**
```typescript
secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET || "dev-secret-change-in-production",
```

The session secret is a well-known default value. This is the EXACT string that appears in dozens of tutorials and boilerplates.

**Impact:** 
- Session cookies can be forged by anyone who knows the secret
- An attacker can impersonate ANY user (including admins) by crafting valid session tokens
- Complete authentication bypass

**Recommendation:** 
1. Generate a cryptographically secure secret: `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(64).toString('hex'))"`
2. Update [.env](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/.env) with the new secret
3. Make the code throw an error in production if the default value is used

