## 🟠 HIGH SEVERITY VULNERABILITIES

---

### HIGH-1: XSS via Email — User Input Injected Directly into HTML

**File: [server/routes.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/routes.ts) (lines 286-296)**
```typescript
// Feedback email — user content directly in HTML without escaping:
<p><strong>From:</strong> ${userName}</p>
<p><strong>Email:</strong> ${userEmail}</p>
<blockquote ...>${feedback.trim()}</blockquote>
```

**Also in:** [server/integrations/oxapay/index.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/oxapay/index.ts) (lines 195-196) — email addresses and userIds interpolated directly into HTML emails.

**Also in:** [server/integrations/qbitcoin/index.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/qbitcoin/index.ts) (lines 513-514) — same pattern.

**Impact:** Stored XSS via email. A malicious user can submit feedback containing `<script>` tags or other HTML that executes when an admin views the email in their email client.

**Recommendation:** HTML-escape all user-provided values before interpolating into HTML:
```typescript
function escapeHtml(str: string): string {
  return str.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
}
```

---

### HIGH-2: Model Config Update Route — No Admin Authorization

**File: [server/routes.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/routes.ts) (lines 320-333)**
```typescript
app.put("/api/models", isAuthenticated, async (req, res) => {
    const { models, mainModelId } = req.body;
    if (models && Array.isArray(models)) {
      currentModels = models; // ANY authenticated user can change models for ALL users!
    }
    if (mainModelId && typeof mainModelId === "string") {
      currentMainModelId = mainModelId; // ANY user can change the default model!
    }
```

**Impact:** 
- ANY logged-in user can change the model configuration for the ENTIRE server
- An attacker could redirect all AI routing to a malicious model endpoint
- An attacker could set arbitrary system prompts that extract user data
- Models are stored in-memory, so this affects ALL concurrent users

**Recommendation:** Add an admin role check. Only allow admin users to modify the model configuration.

---

### HIGH-3: OxaPay Webhook Has No Origin Verification

**File: [server/integrations/oxapay/routes.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/oxapay/routes.ts) (lines 121-161)**

The `/api/oxapay/callback` endpoint accepts POST requests from ANY source — no signature verification, no IP allowlist, no shared secret.

```typescript
app.post("/api/oxapay/callback", async (req: Request, res: Response) => {
    // No signature check, no origin verification
    const { trackId, status } = req.body;
    if (normalizedStatus === "paid" || normalizedStatus === "overpaid") {
      await processOxapayPayment(String(trackId), status, payload);
    }
```

**Impact:** An attacker who discovers or brute-forces a valid `trackId` can forge a payment callback and get free credits.

**Recommendation:** 
1. Add IP allowlisting for OxaPay's callback server IPs
2. Implement HMAC signature verification on the callback payload
3. Always verify payment status with OxaPay's API before crediting (server-side check)

---

### HIGH-4: Webhook Verification Bypassed When Secret is Missing

**File: [server/integrations/paddle/index.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/paddle/index.ts) (lines 47-49)**
```typescript
if (!PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
    logger.warn("paddle", "No PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET set — skipping signature verification");
    return true; // ← Allows ALL unsigned webhooks!
}
```

**File: [server/integrations/lemonsqueezy/index.ts](file:///Users/mac/Documents/Metallm-AI-Aggregator/server/integrations/lemonsqueezy/index.ts) (lines 122-125)**
```typescript
if (!LS_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
    logger.warn("lemonsqueezy", "No LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET set — skipping verification");
    return true; // ← Same problem!
}
```

**Impact:** If webhook secret env vars are accidentally unset/cleared in production deployment, ALL webhook requests are silently accepted without any verification. Attacker can forge payment webhooks and get unlimited free credits.

**Recommendation:** In production, if the webhook secret is missing, REJECT all webhooks (return `false`) instead of accepting them.

