## 🛡️ SERVER & DOMAIN HARDENING RECOMMENDATIONS

### For Server `163.192.155.221`

| # | Recommendation | Priority |
|---|---------------|----------|
| 1 | **Firewall**: Only expose ports 80 (HTTP), 443 (HTTPS), 22 (SSH). Block all others | HIGH |
| 2 | **SSH**: Disable password auth, use SSH key-only authentication | HIGH |
| 3 | **Fail2ban**: Install to auto-block brute-force SSH and HTTP attempts | HIGH |
| 4 | **OS Updates**: Keep all packages updated (`apt update && apt upgrade`) | HIGH |
| 5 | **Node Process**: Run behind Nginx/Caddy reverse proxy, not exposed directly | MED |
| 6 | **Docker**: Consider containerizing the app with non-root user | MED |
| 7 | **Backups**: Automated daily database backups with encryption | MED |
| 8 | **Monitoring**: Set up uptime monitoring (Uptime Kuma, Grafana, etc.) | MED |
| 9 | **Log Rotation**: Configure log rotation to prevent disk space exhaustion | LOW |

### For Domain `metallm.tech`

| # | Recommendation | Priority |
|---|---------------|----------|
| 1 | **SSL/TLS**: Verify Let's Encrypt cert is auto-renewing, test with `ssllabs.com` | HIGH |
| 2 | **HSTS**: Confirm `Strict-Transport-Security` header is set (helmet does this) | HIGH |
| 3 | **DNS CAA**: Add CAA records to restrict who can issue certs for your domain | MED |
| 4 | **DNSSEC**: Enable if your registrar and DNS provider support it | MED |
| 5 | **Subresource Integrity**: Add SRI hashes for external CSS/JS (Google Fonts) | LOW |

